Translation patch: libsignal_core::curve::PublicKey::scalar_is_in_range

Change: the comparison `k[1..31] == [0xFFu8; 30]` becomes `k[1..31] == [0xFFu8; 30][..]`, so it compares a slice with a slice instead of a slice with an array.
Why: Aeneas's Lean standard library models `<[T] as PartialEq<[U]>>::eq` and `<[T; N] as PartialEq<[U; N]>>::eq`, but not `<[T] as PartialEq<[U; N]>>::eq`. The extraction therefore declares `Slice.Insts.CoreCmpPartialEqArray.eq` as an axiom, and the closure of `pqxdh_accept` depends on it through `PublicKey::is_canonical`.
Behaviour: same Boolean. At the pinned rustc, `<[T] as PartialEq<[U; N]>>::eq` returns `false` unless `self.as_array::<N>()` succeeds, which needs the slice to have length `N`, and otherwise compares the two arrays (library/core/src/array/equality.rs). `<[T] as PartialEq<[U]>>::eq` returns `false` on unequal lengths and otherwise compares element by element (library/core/src/slice/cmp.rs). The right-hand side `[0xFFu8; 30][..]` has length 30, and the left-hand side `k[1..31]` has length 30.

diff --git a/rust/core/src/curve.rs b/rust/core/src/curve.rs
--- a/rust/core/src/curve.rs
+++ b/rust/core/src/curve.rs
@@ -180,7 +180,7 @@ impl PublicKey {
                 // specifically, it is not true that either the high bit is set
                 // or that the high 247 bits are all 1 and the bottom byte is >(2^8 - 19)
                 !(k[31] & 0b1000_0000_u8 != 0
-                    || (k[0] >= 0u8.wrapping_sub(19) && k[1..31] == [0xFFu8; 30] && k[31] == 0x7F))
+                    || (k[0] >= 0u8.wrapping_sub(19) && k[1..31] == [0xFFu8; 30][..] && k[31] == 0x7F))
             }
         }
     }
